---
title: Thai Peanut Noodles
description: Rice noodles tossed in a quick creamy peanut-soy-lime sauce, finished with peanuts and herbs.
source: https://tornadoughalli.com/thai-peanut-noodles/
author: Tornadough Alli
servings: 4
prep time: 7 minutes
cook time: 8 minutes
time required: 15 minutes
course: dinner
cuisine: Thai-inspired
tags:
  - noodles
  - peanut
  - quick
  - vegetarian
---

> Adapted from Tornadough Alli. For creamier sauce, swap pasta water for 2 tbsp coconut milk. Lo mein or fettuccine work if you skip rinsing.

Cook @rice noodles{6%oz}(about a 6–6.3 oz package) per package directions, about ~{5-6%minutes}. Reserve @pasta water{2%tbsp}, then drain, rinse, and toss in a #large bowl{} with @sesame oil{1%tbsp}. Set aside.

In a #saucepan{} over medium-low heat, whisk @creamy peanut butter{1/3%cup}, @soy sauce{3%tbsp}, @lime juice{2%tbsp}(fresh), @brown sugar{2%tbsp}, remaining @sesame oil{1%tbsp}, and @chili paste{1%tsp} until smooth, about ~{2%minutes}.

Whisk in the reserved warm pasta water to thin slightly; remove from heat.

Add the noodles and toss until completely coated. Top with @roasted peanuts{2%tbsp}(unsalted, chopped), @green onions{2%tbsp}(sliced), and @fresh cilantro{}(chopped). Serve.
